Revision history for lib-absolute

{{$NEXT}}
  - Ship a Changes file, so the release tests have a changelog to check and
    the next release has a section to stamp.
  - Ship a LICENSE file with the Perl 5 licence text, so the distribution
    builds again and GitHub detects the licence of the repository.
  - Declare the prerequisites in a cpanfile instead of dist.ini, so the
    requirements have exactly one source.
  - The error of "use lib::absolute -hard" now names the @INC entry that
    failed besides the absolute path it resolved to, so a caller can tell
    which of their entries is broken.
